{
  "sim_type": "excel",
  "title": "Navigate the Grid: TCS Quarterly Data Entry and Movement",
  "scenario": "You're an analyst at a Mumbai equity desk. TCS has just released its quarterly financials (Q1–Q4 FY24), and you need to populate a tracking sheet with revenue, profit, and tax data. Your supervisor expects clean navigation, zero entry errors, and proper cell selection — she'll review the sheet in 10 minutes. Use keyboard motion (arrow keys, Ctrl+arrows, selection ranges) and data entry discipline to build and audit the input block.",
  "instructions": "Enter the TCS quarterly financial data into the grid using keyboard navigation only (no mouse clicks except to open the file). Then use selection ranges to validate totals and verify three calculations in the Answers sheet. Save the workbook after each major entry block.",
  "learning_objective": "Navigate a multi-row data entry task using Ctrl+arrows and Shift+selection, enter numeric and text data with precision, select ranges to audit totals via the status bar, and build a simple validation check using SUM formulas.",
  "hints": [
    "Press Ctrl+Home to return to A1 after any jump. Use Ctrl+Shift+Down to select an entire data block and check its Sum in the status bar.",
    "In row 1, type the headers: Fiscal Year, Revenue, Net Profit, Tax Rate, Cash Generated. Use Tab to move right and Enter to confirm. Then use Ctrl+Down to jump to the last row of headers before entering data.",
    "After entering all data, click cell B12 and type =SUM(B2:B11) to verify total revenue. The status bar will also show the sum if you select B2:B11 — compare them to catch entry errors."
  ],
